      "writtenOn": "2025-04-23T11:13:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure, as currently `PipelineCachingTests.cpp` already test frontend and blob cache with and without isolation key [1], and the backend shader compilation blob cache key already contains isolation key (from `Device::GetCacheKey()` [2]) so the tested behavior have no change with this CL. (Actually I am not quite sure where the pipeline blob cache key includes the isolation key, but it seems they did)\n\nI think this CL targeted at underlying drivers\u0027 compilation cache, e.g. D3D12 driver cache the result from compiled DXIL to actual ISA code, but that could go beyond Dawn\u0027s domain.\n\nMaybe we could add end-to-end tests to see devices with different isolation key yield different HLSL/MSL/SPIRV code?\n\n[1]: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/tests/end2end/PipelineCachingTests.cpp;drc\u003db6620a02fa498df5297e53241b54a31f488ca440;l\u003d274\n[2]:https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/CacheRequest.h;l\u003d95;drc\u003db6620a02fa498df5297e53241b54a31f488ca440",
      "parentUuid": "5118dae7_2557bd10",
      "revId": "5f07faa78e73ce54780be7ce918565e3b1f6eb89",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a8ea931_67b8c6ae",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Device.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 386,
