      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-22T15:23:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should already be an unguessable token so why do we need to hash it?",
      "revId": "5f07faa78e73ce54780be7ce918565e3b1f6eb89",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "56c374b7_f0a0d2de",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Device.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 386,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-22T18:45:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is from Chromium, but since it\u0027s passed into Dawn as a `wgpu::StringView` it doesn\u0027t always have to be a unguessable token. I think hashing it here is fine to make it work everywhere else also.",
      "parentUuid": "9a8ea931_67b8c6ae",
      "revId": "5f07faa78e73ce54780be7ce918565e3b1f6eb89",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6ecc5e58_21bddacd",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Device.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 386,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-23T11:00:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Even if not unguessable, what do we gain from hashing? If the token can be known, then the hash of it will be known as well. We are not gaining anything from hashing, except maybe getting from a variable length string (maybe too long) to a fixed, known, large length.",
      "parentUuid": "56c374b7_f0a0d2de",
      "revId": "5f07faa78e73ce54780be7ce918565e3b1f6eb89",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6bbe65fe_b96e1de7",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Device.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 386,
      "author": {
        "id": 3874508
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-23T11:13:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, and I think hashing it can free us from having any assumption for key or handle any special char (space, dash, etc...)?",
      "parentUuid": "56c374b7_f0a0d2de",
      "revId": "5f07faa78e73ce54780be7ce918565e3b1f6eb89",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
